== r3.90 (B1): FormatFloat(F, Decimals) (Std.Strings) writes F with exactly
== Decimals digits after the point, 0..20, rounded to nearest from the exact
== binary value; no point when Decimals is 0. A Float32 is widened exactly.
Use Std.Strings

Main :
    Price Float := 19.987
    Small Float32 := 0.1
    PutLn(FormatFloat(Price, 2), " ", FormatFloat(Price, 0), " ", FormatFloat(Price, 5), " ", FormatFloat(-1.0 / 3.0, 3))
    PutLn(FormatFloat(Small, 10), " ", FormatFloat(1.0e20, 1), " ", FormatFloat(0.0, 2), " [", FormatFloat(7.0, 0), "]")
    PutLn(FormatFloat(Price, 21))
;
